## Lore

The zembahk, the mystic worms, come from a world the Splugorth conquered. They look like a length of intestine or a giant fleshy pink worm with a single large white eye, no mouth and no apparent ears, and they feed on tiny amounts of magic energy. They are gentle, peaceful beings who once lived in harmony with nature, surrounded by beauty and art, with a simple, almost childlike view of the world that seeks goodness, happiness and comfort and cares nothing for possessions, money or power.

That changed when the Splugorth found them. A zembahk carries enormous reserves of P.P.E. and I.S.P., making it an ideal power source for bio-wizardry, and it can instill abilities into a device whether or not it knows the spell. Conversion lobotomizes the creature or kills it. The Splugorth breed them, hold billions in stasis, raid their homeworld for fresh stock and have seeded other planets with them as unwitting breeding colonies, and they guard the homeworld''s location jealously. Zembahk are not dimensional travelers, so they are very rare elsewhere, but escapees turn up wherever the Splugorth have a colony, Earth included. The cover of the book shows a lobotomized zembahk as the heart of a staff of pacification.

They rely on instinct, empathy and psionic perception rather than science or machines, and use their innate magic and psionics for transport, building and defense. They are friendly, kind, adventurous and very curious about other life.

Alignment: any, but usually principled, scrupulous or unprincipled. Weight 6 to 10 lbs (2.7 to 4.5 kg); length 3 to 5 ft (0.9 to 1.5 m). Average experience level 1D4. Average life span 300 years, half or less as a bio-wizard component. Slave market value 400,000 to 600,000 credits.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'zembahk');


